.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_GET_FIELD_TYPE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_get_field_type ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_get_ec_point_conv_form
.Nd get field type or point conversion form of a key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_get_field_type
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_get_ec_point_conv_form
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_field_type
returns the field type NID of the
.Fa pkey ,
if
.Fa pkey Ns 's
key type supports it.
The types currently supported by the built-in OpenSSL providers are
either
.Sy NID_X9_62_prime_field
for prime curves or
.Sy NID_X9_62_characteristic_two_field
for binary curves; these values are defined in the
.Pa <openssl/obj_mac.h>
header file.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_ec_point_conv_form
returns the point conversion format of the
.Fa pkey ,
if
.Fa pkey Ns 's
key type supports it.
.Sh NOTES
Among the standard OpenSSL key types, this is only supported for EC and
SM2 keys.
Other providers may support this for additional key types.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_field_type
returns the field type NID or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_ec_point_conv_form
returns the point conversion format number (see
.Xr EC_GROUP_copy 3 )
or 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EC_GROUP_copy 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
